00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:07,109
Hess's law also lets us find the lattice enthalpy of an ionic solid, which can never be measured directly.

2
00:00:07,109 --> 00:00:10,651
This is the Born Haber cycle for sodium chloride.

3
00:00:10,651 --> 00:00:13,645
Start from sodium metal and chlorine gas.

4
00:00:13,645 --> 00:00:17,395
Turn sodium into a gas: plus one oh eight.

5
00:00:17,395 --> 00:00:23,554
Break half a mole of chlorine bonds: half of two forty two, plus one twenty one.

